 "equipment_type": "VRF water-cooled outdoor unit monitoring via BACnet gateway",
 "applies_to": "Daikin water-cooled VRV units VRV-3W-WATER (RWEYQ8-30P), VRV3C2-WATER (RWEYP***PCTJ), VRV-3Wx-WATER (RWEYQ8-30P) and VRV-4W-WATER (RWEYQ8-10T7Y1B) read through a CoolAutomation gateway with PRO functionality.",
 "summary": "With PRO functionality, CoolAutomation gateways publish service data from each Daikin VRV-3W/4W water-cooled outdoor unit over BACnet: AirNet address, HP, suction, discharge, coil, subcooling, EV liquid pipe, evaporating and condensing temperatures, EV openings, inverter speed, fin temperature and current, compressor, heater, valve, pump and cooling-fan states, retry and stepping-down flags and fan step (40 objects). Monitoring only.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": 64,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Instance = VA x 256 + index (object identifier bits 21-8 = VA, 7-0 = index). Points shown for VA 1; the guide does not explain how outdoor units receive their VA.",
  "Access set to read-only: these are measured service values, although the guide's type table lists PIV as read/write.",
  "Object names are the guide's short names; descriptions are the guide's object descriptions with the bracketed unit moved to units.",
  "Table printed on page 45 of the guide (section 3.2.1.3).",
  "For the outdoor system objects the guide groups these series with VRV-M (REYQ8-48M), VRV-3R and VRV3C; that table matches site lists coolmasternet-daikin-vrv-system-vrvm-reyq8-48m and coolmasternet-daikin-vrv-system-vrv3r-vrv3c."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "BACnet Integration Guidelines - CoolMaster Product Line, CooLinkNet, CooLinkHub, CooLinkBridge",
